Subject: [PATCH 02593/11362] [conductor] In-process docs for PHASE C
 (CONTINUOUS SELF-LEARNING; mandated per research-program.md; the LOCALIZER
 compounds; verifier_is_oracle=false) -- does the verifiable-process-data
 LOCALIZER SELF-IMPROVE / COMPOUND as labeled first-error traces accumulate?
 The .405 detector COMPOUNDED but WEAKLY (exp4385: localization-F1
 0.371->0.387, AUROC saturated 0.986 -- little headroom). The .406 localizer
 (exp4392) has REAL headroom (the ensemble baseline is F1 0.096). Apply the
 exp4364/exp4385 compounding-curve discipline to the localizer: as
 verifiable-synthetic + REAL first-error labels accumulate, measure held-out
 first-error localization-F1 vs the accumulated-corpus SIZE (a
 monotone-improving learning curve), reproduction-gated, with a POSITIVE
 CONTROL (a from-scratch localizer on the full corpus = the ceiling) and a
 NO-LEARNING baseline (the .405 ensemble detector, F1 0.096). Emit
 localizer_compounds BARE bool := (held-out first-error localization-F1 rises
 with corpus size BEYOND the no-learning baseline, delta CI95-excl-0, AND the
 positive control confirms non-trivial ceiling headroom).
 verifier_is_oracle=false. A win = the localizer vehicle COMPOUNDS (it gets
 better with first-error data -- the self-learning headline on the axis that
 now has real headroom); a CLEAN null (the localizer saturates early) is
 decision-grade. If exp4392 built no localizer, FALL BACK to the
 ensemble-detector localization-compounding reading. Cached candidates, CPU,
 zero quota. NO TRM training.

